# Repository-root build context. Only `web/Dockerfile` builds from here
# (`.github/workflows/docker-web.yaml` sets `context: .`); hub, lab and helper
# build from their own directories and carry their own .dockerignore.
#
# `npm ci` inside the build stage populates web/node_modules for linux/amd64;
# without these rules the host's own node_modules (possibly built for another
# architecture) and a stale web/dist would be uploaded into the context and
# copied straight over it by `COPY web/ web/`.
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/.venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.vite/
.git/
.github/
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
data/
docs/
*.log
